WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.920 --> 00:00:03.480
- [Mark] All right, Elizabeth.

00:00:03.480 --> 00:00:04.313
- Yes, sir.

00:00:04.313 --> 00:00:05.270
- [Mark] Elizabeth, where'd you grow up?

00:00:05.270 --> 00:00:06.417
Where you from originally?

00:00:06.417 --> 00:00:08.630
- [Elizabeth] Olive Branch, Mississippi.

00:00:08.630 --> 00:00:09.990
- [Mark] And tell me about your childhood.

00:00:09.990 --> 00:00:11.862
You had both your parents
when you were young?

00:00:11.862 --> 00:00:15.612
- [Elizabeth] I did to start off with.

00:00:15.612 --> 00:00:20.612
My dad left, you know, when
I was around two or three,

00:00:21.594 --> 00:00:24.190
four or five, I guess.

00:00:24.190 --> 00:00:26.820
He kept coming around for a little bit

00:00:26.820 --> 00:00:29.640
and I was actually molested

00:00:29.640 --> 00:00:33.710
by my dad from about three to six.

00:00:33.710 --> 00:00:34.660
- [Mark] I'm sorry.

00:00:37.240 --> 00:00:41.580
- Other than that, I had
a, my mom she's a nurse.

00:00:41.580 --> 00:00:43.400
I had a good childhood.

00:00:43.400 --> 00:00:46.983
I was raised, you know, my
mom and my grandparents.

00:00:46.983 --> 00:00:50.630
Things were pretty good, pretty normal,

00:00:50.630 --> 00:00:52.840
you know, other than my dad.

00:00:52.840 --> 00:00:57.463
And then he left and
stayed gone, you know.

00:00:59.300 --> 00:01:03.823
I still to this day, don't
see him, you know, very often.

00:01:07.570 --> 00:01:09.977
I remember like riding
four wheelers, you know,

00:01:09.977 --> 00:01:12.900
and just grew up out in the
country, everything normal.

00:01:12.900 --> 00:01:15.640
I went to school, everything was good

00:01:17.140 --> 00:01:21.270
but I always remember
feeling like I wasn't enough.

00:01:21.270 --> 00:01:22.450
It wasn't-

00:01:22.450 --> 00:01:23.860
- [Mark] Did you have
that feeling before you

00:01:23.860 --> 00:01:27.093
were raped, molested or
did it start after that?

00:01:27.093 --> 00:01:30.300
- I think it started after
that, more when I grew

00:01:30.300 --> 00:01:32.683
into my teenage years, yeah.

00:01:34.210 --> 00:01:35.260
- [Mark] Did you ever confront your dad

00:01:35.260 --> 00:01:37.320
or say anything to your mom or anybody?

00:01:37.320 --> 00:01:41.160
- I did to my mom when
I was 18 and, you know,

00:01:41.160 --> 00:01:43.009
she didn't know.

00:01:43.009 --> 00:01:47.453
I mean, and you know by then my thing is,

00:01:48.463 --> 00:01:51.830
I don't live to hate
anybody, so I don't hate him.

00:01:51.830 --> 00:01:54.915
I forgive him. I have to
remember he's sick too.

00:01:54.915 --> 00:01:55.748
- [Mark] Yeah.

00:01:55.748 --> 00:01:59.820
- Especially with me being
like this, like I know

00:01:59.820 --> 00:02:03.593
that you know, we all deal
with some kind of demons.

00:02:06.030 --> 00:02:09.411
- [Mark] Yeah. And then how
far do you go in school?

00:02:09.411 --> 00:02:13.130
- I went to, my 11th
grade year I dropped out

00:02:13.130 --> 00:02:17.680
and then I got a GED and
I did a year of college,

00:02:17.680 --> 00:02:20.380
a year of nursing school, actually.

00:02:20.380 --> 00:02:25.380
And then I had my first
son which is Landon

00:02:25.670 --> 00:02:29.410
and I wanted to stay at home with him.

00:02:29.410 --> 00:02:32.220
So, I stayed at home with him.

00:02:32.220 --> 00:02:35.313
His dad was a plumber, you know,

00:02:36.241 --> 00:02:38.370
and he took care of everything.

00:02:38.370 --> 00:02:41.550
Even though we did drugs, I
stayed at home with my child

00:02:41.550 --> 00:02:46.170
and did 'em, you know, and
I know that sounds horrible

00:02:46.170 --> 00:02:47.360
but that's-

00:02:47.360 --> 00:02:49.273
- [Mark] How the drugs
come into your life?

00:02:50.398 --> 00:02:53.970
- I think being around the
wrong people, you know,

00:02:53.970 --> 00:02:57.463
the people your mom and them
tell you to stay away from.

00:03:01.020 --> 00:03:04.451
They were older than me and
they were doing something

00:03:04.451 --> 00:03:07.620
and I wanted to know what it was like.

00:03:07.620 --> 00:03:10.400
- [Mark] Yeah. Did you
find that the drugs kind

00:03:11.759 --> 00:03:15.568
of numb the pain of what
you went through as a child?

00:03:15.568 --> 00:03:17.550
- They do. They do.

00:03:17.550 --> 00:03:21.035
It numbs every, well it
did, it numbed everything.

00:03:21.035 --> 00:03:22.081
- [Mark] Made everything okay?

00:03:22.081 --> 00:03:24.542
- It made everything okay.

00:03:24.542 --> 00:03:25.980
Made everything normal.

00:03:25.980 --> 00:03:28.910
Everybody was happy or I was happy,

00:03:28.910 --> 00:03:31.470
you know, I thought that-

00:03:31.470 --> 00:03:32.303
- [Mark] Yeah.

00:03:32.303 --> 00:03:35.298
- In reality, it's miserable.

00:03:35.298 --> 00:03:36.272
- [Mark] Yeah.

00:03:36.272 --> 00:03:37.105
- Miserable.

00:03:37.105 --> 00:03:39.553
- [Mark] And then how did
prostitution come into your life?

00:03:41.390 --> 00:03:43.720
- I've always had my
son's dad to take care

00:03:43.720 --> 00:03:45.570
of me and to take care of everything.

00:03:46.530 --> 00:03:51.233
Right at two years ago, he
passed away from an overdose.

00:03:54.972 --> 00:03:58.627
And that's when I actually
started prostitution.

00:03:58.627 --> 00:04:00.369
- [Mark] Because he needed the money?

00:04:00.369 --> 00:04:03.253
- Because I needed the
money to support my habit.

00:04:05.540 --> 00:04:06.640
- [Mark] And your son?

00:04:07.890 --> 00:04:11.780
- Well, in actuality I
don't take care of my son.

00:04:11.780 --> 00:04:13.290
- [Mark] Oh, where is he?

00:04:13.290 --> 00:04:14.663
- He's with my mom.

00:04:17.740 --> 00:04:20.423
Sorry. It's okay.

00:04:27.331 --> 00:04:30.498
I don't wanna talk about that, sorry.

00:04:34.580 --> 00:04:36.340
- [Mark] So sex work started for you

00:04:36.340 --> 00:04:39.210
and you worked on your own or with a pimp?

00:04:39.210 --> 00:04:40.710
- I started with a pimp

00:04:42.830 --> 00:04:47.010
and I saw that I was giving
these people way more money

00:04:47.010 --> 00:04:50.970
then what I was getting out of it.

00:04:50.970 --> 00:04:54.540
I mean, I wasn't getting
literally anything but drugs.

00:04:54.540 --> 00:04:59.540
I wasn't being taken care of
in any type of way, you know.

00:05:00.957 --> 00:05:02.630
I was still struggling by myself,

00:05:02.630 --> 00:05:06.790
so I decided I was gonna go struggle

00:05:06.790 --> 00:05:11.213
by myself and not come into Midtown.

00:05:14.566 --> 00:05:16.920
And I just started on my own.

00:05:16.920 --> 00:05:20.900
But you still, you still
had to pay for protection

00:05:20.900 --> 00:05:24.883
you know, you have to have
a place to stay every night.

00:05:26.070 --> 00:05:26.903
- [Mark] Were you able to get away

00:05:26.903 --> 00:05:27.930
from that pimp relationship?

00:05:27.930 --> 00:05:30.757
- I was, it was actually, he,

00:05:34.900 --> 00:05:37.570
still to this day I deal with him

00:05:37.570 --> 00:05:40.850
and I still have to pay him
when I see him and stuff

00:05:40.850 --> 00:05:44.330
but I was actually able to leave.

00:05:44.330 --> 00:05:46.360
- [Mark] How did you do that?

00:05:46.360 --> 00:05:49.023
- I just walked away one day and,

00:05:50.470 --> 00:05:51.973
you know, I got,

00:05:54.470 --> 00:05:59.470
I was kidnapped over
it and raped and beat.

00:06:02.230 --> 00:06:05.677
And after that, nothing, you know.

00:06:05.677 --> 00:06:08.127
- [Mark] But you still
continue to pay him today?

00:06:11.340 --> 00:06:16.190
Just because you're in his territory, or?

00:06:16.190 --> 00:06:18.643
- When I'm in his territory, yes.

00:06:20.444 --> 00:06:24.370
- [Mark] And the guys that, your customers

00:06:24.370 --> 00:06:29.123
the guys that pay you, they
treat you nicely, they're,

00:06:30.880 --> 00:06:32.410
how do you get treated by them?

00:06:32.410 --> 00:06:33.663
- Most of them do.

00:06:36.807 --> 00:06:40.023
You know, you have some that,

00:06:41.970 --> 00:06:44.320
they take advantage of this situation.

00:06:44.320 --> 00:06:48.703
They will rape you, they will
take your money, you know.

00:06:52.185 --> 00:06:53.630
- [Mark] Do you get depressed sometimes?

00:06:53.630 --> 00:06:57.173
- Do I get depressed? I stay depressed.

00:06:59.770 --> 00:07:04.260
And that's why I still, you
know, I do the heroin now

00:07:04.260 --> 00:07:07.710
'cause my body physically has to have it.

00:07:07.710 --> 00:07:12.260
But, it's like the more I do

00:07:12.260 --> 00:07:14.760
the more miserable I am, you know,

00:07:14.760 --> 00:07:18.523
it's like a never ending
cycle of just madness.

00:07:23.160 --> 00:07:25.410
- [Mark] And are you making enough money

00:07:25.410 --> 00:07:27.873
to support yourself or your habits?

00:07:31.130 --> 00:07:33.033
- Most of the time I do.

00:07:34.010 --> 00:07:36.070
Sometimes I don't, you know,

00:07:36.070 --> 00:07:39.380
sometimes I don't have a place to stay.

00:07:39.380 --> 00:07:41.033
Sometimes I don't have all the dubs

00:07:41.033 --> 00:07:43.683
that I need to keep me
well through the day.

00:07:46.000 --> 00:07:48.000
I mean, it just depends.

00:07:48.900 --> 00:07:51.663
I do pretty well, most of the time.

00:07:53.960 --> 00:07:55.630
- [Mark] And do you still
have contact with your family?

00:07:55.630 --> 00:07:56.843
- I do. I do.

00:07:58.230 --> 00:08:00.060
- [Mark] They know what
you're going through and?

00:08:00.060 --> 00:08:03.920
- Yeah. Well, I mean they know

00:08:03.920 --> 00:08:08.530
but we don't talk about it like, you know.

00:08:08.530 --> 00:08:11.480
It was always in my household,
when there's a problem,

00:08:11.480 --> 00:08:14.653
you push it under the rug
and it just goes away.

00:08:15.520 --> 00:08:18.823
But this is not going away, you know.

00:08:20.720 --> 00:08:23.090
This is real, true life.

00:08:23.090 --> 00:08:24.563
- [Mark] Do you see a way out?

00:08:25.760 --> 00:08:27.883
- Right now, honestly no.

00:08:35.580 --> 00:08:37.290
- [Mark] So you have one child, right?

00:08:37.290 --> 00:08:38.610
- I have two children.

00:08:38.610 --> 00:08:40.430
I have a 19 month old

00:08:42.130 --> 00:08:45.043
that was adopted by a family in Memphis.

00:08:50.575 --> 00:08:53.175
- [Mark] And who is the
father of your second child?

00:08:55.720 --> 00:08:57.470
- He used to be a customer of mine.

00:09:00.757 --> 00:09:03.663
And we actually got into a relationship

00:09:06.540 --> 00:09:11.540
but it was just not, not a good situation,

00:09:12.540 --> 00:09:14.963
you know, very bad enabler.

00:09:18.110 --> 00:09:20.363
Very controlling, you know.

00:09:22.420 --> 00:09:26.840
In one form or another,
I'm always getting beat on

00:09:26.840 --> 00:09:30.200
or raped or, you know, just-

00:09:30.200 --> 00:09:32.050
- [Mark] It must be hard,
'cause everyone in your life

00:09:32.050 --> 00:09:34.270
is trying to take advantage of you?

00:09:34.270 --> 00:09:35.583
- That's how, yes. That's how I've-

00:09:35.583 --> 00:09:37.710
- [Mark] They're just using
you one way or another.

00:09:37.710 --> 00:09:38.780
- Pretty much.

00:09:38.780 --> 00:09:42.530
- [Mark] And that's gotta
undermine your self worth on top

00:09:42.530 --> 00:09:44.608
of what you've already went
through as a young girl?

00:09:44.608 --> 00:09:45.624
- [Elizabeth] Right.

00:09:45.624 --> 00:09:46.874
- [Mark] Right?

00:09:51.580 --> 00:09:53.788
What helps you survive this?

00:09:53.788 --> 00:09:54.621
- [Elizabeth] What?

00:09:54.621 --> 00:09:57.873
- [Mark] You must be very
strong to continue doing this.

00:09:58.910 --> 00:10:00.210
What helps you survive it?

00:10:02.826 --> 00:10:05.540
- [Elizabeth] I honestly don't know.

00:10:05.540 --> 00:10:09.290
The thought of my child
living with no parents,

00:10:09.290 --> 00:10:10.940
that's my only thing.

00:10:12.603 --> 00:10:15.260
I mean, 'cause I still see him and stuff,

00:10:15.260 --> 00:10:17.010
you know, just about every weekend.

00:10:18.960 --> 00:10:21.310
But just the thought of, you know,

00:10:21.310 --> 00:10:23.350
losing his dad was enough.

00:10:23.350 --> 00:10:26.110
What if he lost both of us?

00:10:26.110 --> 00:10:28.246
But if I don't get off of this,

00:10:28.246 --> 00:10:32.583
he might as well not have
me because I'm not there.

00:10:36.760 --> 00:10:38.293
- [Mark] You've been arrested before?

00:10:39.581 --> 00:10:41.883
- [Elizabeth] Yes, once for a DUI.

00:10:43.370 --> 00:10:46.400
Other than that, I try
to stay out of the way.

00:10:46.400 --> 00:10:50.160
I respect 'em, they have a job to do.

00:10:50.160 --> 00:10:51.887
And that's what they're doing.

00:10:51.887 --> 00:10:53.573
And I'm doing something wrong.

00:10:55.830 --> 00:10:57.780
- [Mark] How much do you make in a day?

00:10:59.490 --> 00:11:02.610
- [Elizabeth] Anywhere from 250 to $1,500.

00:11:11.229 --> 00:11:13.560
- [Mark] On a good night, you making 1500.

00:11:13.560 --> 00:11:15.420
You end up keeping how much of that?

00:11:16.920 --> 00:11:18.443
- I mean, what do you mean, after-

00:11:18.443 --> 00:11:21.367
- [Mark] Like you're giving
away some of it to the pimp.

00:11:21.367 --> 00:11:26.367
- I mean, I don't go give him, you know,

00:11:26.530 --> 00:11:31.050
say out of 1500, he might get two, 200.

00:11:31.050 --> 00:11:33.290
- [Mark] Yeah. So that's fairly
good money on a good night.

00:11:33.290 --> 00:11:34.123
- Yeah.

00:11:36.780 --> 00:11:38.950
- [Mark] And yet you're still struggling?

00:11:38.950 --> 00:11:43.950
- I mean, I have a $300
a day dope habit, almost.

00:11:45.280 --> 00:11:47.100
Right now, that means-

00:11:47.100 --> 00:11:49.000
- [Mark] You gotta keep that up.

00:11:49.000 --> 00:11:54.000
And then, you know, a place
to live, you know, food.

00:11:57.400 --> 00:11:59.940
Some days we go without eating.

00:11:59.940 --> 00:12:03.807
Some days I don't make
anything if I don't feel,

00:12:03.807 --> 00:12:05.743
you know, I don't make anything.

00:12:07.190 --> 00:12:08.670
- [Mark] How do you feel
like this has changed you?

00:12:08.670 --> 00:12:11.510
This life, working the streets and-

00:12:11.510 --> 00:12:14.353
- I feel like it has broke me as a person.

00:12:16.130 --> 00:12:20.343
I feel less than even
more than I did before.

00:12:29.866 --> 00:12:34.153
I feel very, I feel like I'm
just existing in this world.

00:12:40.930 --> 00:12:45.010
- [Mark] How do you feel about
the, the men that pay you?

00:12:45.010 --> 00:12:45.843
Do you respect them?

00:12:45.843 --> 00:12:48.653
Are they good guys or you just-

00:12:49.807 --> 00:12:51.597
- I just do my job.

00:12:51.597 --> 00:12:53.143
- [Mark] You're just using
them and they're using you?

00:12:54.630 --> 00:12:55.463
- Right.

00:13:01.030 --> 00:13:04.100
- [Mark] What advice would
you give to someone else

00:13:04.100 --> 00:13:06.720
that's in your situation
and considering doing

00:13:06.720 --> 00:13:08.050
this kind of work?

00:13:08.050 --> 00:13:09.337
- Don't. Don't.

00:13:13.874 --> 00:13:17.343
Anything has to be better than this.

00:13:19.818 --> 00:13:22.330
Like, I mean, what comes along with it?

00:13:22.330 --> 00:13:27.330
The abuse, you know, when I was directly

00:13:27.750 --> 00:13:30.016
with the pimp, if I were to make $1,500

00:13:30.016 --> 00:13:32.395
I would've had to take it directly to him.

00:13:32.395 --> 00:13:33.540
- [Mark] All of it?

00:13:33.540 --> 00:13:34.963
- All of it, right.

00:13:36.512 --> 00:13:41.512
You know, don't, that's
all I can say is, don't.

00:13:48.160 --> 00:13:51.860
- [Mark] What's the most
important lesson you've learned?

00:13:55.173 --> 00:13:57.370
- I think to watch out for yourself

00:13:57.370 --> 00:14:00.323
because nobody's gonna
watch out for you like you.

00:14:03.327 --> 00:14:05.033
You know, value your family.

00:14:10.900 --> 00:14:11.870
- [Mark] How old are you?

00:14:11.870 --> 00:14:12.703
- I'm 30.

00:14:18.330 --> 00:14:20.963
- [Mark] What's your biggest
regret, losing your kids?

00:14:23.550 --> 00:14:28.540
- Yes, I have two actually.

00:14:28.540 --> 00:14:33.540
My son's dad dying due to drug, you know.

00:14:35.160 --> 00:14:36.798
I wish I had of been there.

00:14:36.798 --> 00:14:38.348
I wish I could have stopped it.

00:14:40.150 --> 00:14:42.673
Having to give my child up for adoption.

00:14:43.550 --> 00:14:46.100
- [Mark] It's gotta be so
hard for a mother, right?

00:14:50.057 --> 00:14:52.443
- And my other son and having, you know,

00:14:52.443 --> 00:14:55.526
losing his dad and me being out here.

00:14:57.563 --> 00:15:00.540
- [Mark] Do you feel like
the, the sexual abuse

00:15:00.540 --> 00:15:04.780
as a child kind of set the whole chain

00:15:04.780 --> 00:15:08.240
of destruction's, got
that started for you?

00:15:08.240 --> 00:15:10.500
Led to the drug addiction,
led to the sex work,

00:15:10.500 --> 00:15:13.959
led to the situation you're in right now?

00:15:13.959 --> 00:15:15.430
- Maybe some of it,

00:15:15.430 --> 00:15:19.213
or maybe me not dealing
with it, you know, did.

00:15:20.170 --> 00:15:21.130
- [Mark] It's a lot to deal with.

00:15:21.130 --> 00:15:25.470
- You know, they tried
to work me through it

00:15:25.470 --> 00:15:26.840
when I was younger.

00:15:26.840 --> 00:15:30.920
And I think if I would have
done it, you know, maybe.

00:15:30.920 --> 00:15:32.590
- [Mark] You think
therapy might've helped?

00:15:32.590 --> 00:15:33.423
- Maybe.

00:15:33.423 --> 00:15:34.256
- [Mark] Yeah?

00:15:34.256 --> 00:15:35.089
- Yeah.

00:15:36.310 --> 00:15:39.730
If I would've been keen
to actually, you know,

00:15:39.730 --> 00:15:43.720
stuck with it and not let that make me

00:15:43.720 --> 00:15:46.270
as a person because that's not who I am.

00:15:46.270 --> 00:15:48.250
That's just what I've been through.

00:15:52.580 --> 00:15:54.534
- [Mark] All right,
Elizabeth, thank you so much

00:15:54.534 --> 00:15:57.053
for sharing your story and
I wish you the best of luck

00:15:57.053 --> 00:15:58.807
with everything you're going through.

00:15:58.807 --> 00:16:00.990
- [Elizabeth] Thank you.

00:16:00.990 --> 00:16:02.440
- [Mark] Thank you very much.

